# Release archives carry the code only: the calculations/ package and the LICENSE.
# GitHub builds a release's "Source code" zip with `git archive`, which honours export-ignore,
# and Zenodo deposits that zip. Docs, Markdown, studies, notebooks, tests and the container stay
# in the repository and in every clone; they are left out of the archive, not out of git.
#
# Everything is ignored first and the code is let back in. The directory line is needed as
# well as the /** line: an ignored directory is skipped whole, whatever its contents say.
* export-ignore
/calculations -export-ignore
/calculations/** -export-ignore
/LICENSE -export-ignore

# The effect-of sweep notebooks and the study comparison are committed WITHOUT their outputs.
# Their figures are regenerable (the *-results/ folders are already gitignored for that reason),
# and a full re-run rewrites ~190 MB of embedded images, which would land in the history again on
# every commit. The working copy keeps its outputs; only the committed blob is stripped.
#
# The filter is tools/strip_notebook_outputs.py, defined in .gitconfig. Git does not read a
# repository's own config file, so enable it once in any clone you commit from:
#
#   git config --local include.path ../.gitconfig
#
# Without it these lines do nothing and the notebooks are committed with their outputs;
# tests/test_committed_notebooks.py then fails on the staged copies.
*/effect-of-*.ipynb                 filter=strip-outputs
Comparisons/study-comparison.ipynb  filter=strip-outputs
